# Artist promotional photography

- Artist portrait imagery is an **artist-owned media library**, not just a Studio project's temporary attachment. In schema `studio_artist_images` it is linked by `artist_id`, has independent selected state and can optionally retain a `source_asset_id` for provenance.
- New artist photos generated inside Studio attach automatically to the selected artist; artist-only generation is available on the Artists screen without any song project. A project without an assigned artist cannot generate an artist-photo.
- Preserve existing selected Studio images via idempotent migration. Never silently transfer an artist's photo to a different artist if the Studio project's artist changes.
- Deleting a project image must not delete the independently owned artist image or its original file. Artist gallery removal is a separate explicit action; do not destroy project assets.
- Only one selected hero background per artist, with photo variants selectable from the gallery. Preserve the current hero when new variants arrive and do not overwrite it silently.
- Artist banners are wide horizontal 16:9, responsive full width with cover crop and name/genre layered by CSS in the lower-left. Artist names, metadata, badges and stats should never be baked into photo pixels. Never invent Spotify verification/listener metrics.
- Albums use their own square 1:1 artwork and assets. Keep them separate from artist promotional images.
- Check actual image generation, gallery selection, auth and migration with tests before reporting success. `src/chatgpt-images.mjs`, `src/studio.mjs`, `public/app.js`.
